WEBVTT

NOTE
Kind: captions
Source: Articulate Closed Captions Editor
Source Version: 3.103.35301.0

00:00:00.019 --> 00:00:00.920
This is Millie.

00:00:01.139 --> 00:00:05.429
She is sat at her desk feeling overwhelmed by the stacks of tasks she has to do.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:06.960
She feels anxious,

00:00:07.159 --> 00:00:09.739
she can feel the clouds gathering above her head again.

00:00:10.279 --> 00:00:11.829
She doesn't know where to begin.

00:00:12.399 --> 00:00:13.710
Her anxiety rises,

00:00:13.819 --> 00:00:15.270
it all feels too much.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:17.229
Her work feels unmanageable,

00:00:17.399 --> 00:00:18.809
leaving her feeling stuck.

00:00:19.399 --> 00:00:20.469
Millie has an idea.

00:00:20.639 --> 00:00:24.360
She decides to use the Eisenhower matrix to break down her tasks.

00:00:25.069 --> 00:00:27.780
She lists her tasks and puts them into categories,

00:00:27.909 --> 00:00:29.340
urgent and important,

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:31.340
important but not urgent,

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:33.060
urgent but not important,

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:35.150
and not urgent and not important.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:37.970
Now Millie feels more inspired.

00:00:38.259 --> 00:00:42.009
She knows to only focus on the urgent and important tasks today.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:44.700
That way she can build up momentum to tackle

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:48.209
tasks from the important but not urgent pile tomorrow.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:53.290
Millie has reached the end of the day and has made great progress on a few of her tasks.

00:00:53.459 --> 00:00:56.209
It doesn't matter that they didn't all get accomplished today.

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:58.549
Progress doesn't have a set speed.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:00.290
As long as you're making progress,

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:01.580
that's all that matters.

